ostrya (0.6.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Push, push-tree, and pull with a bucket repository in an S3 bucket.
    Add remote init, remote fsck, remote prune, remote summary -u, push
    --break-lock, and the --s3-* options.
  * Sign and verify RSA, ECDSA P-384, and Ed25519 keys under spki. Read
    the spki key files as PEM blocks. Refuse the raw spki key forms and
    the r || s signature.
  * Apply --sign-type to the keys after it.
  * Refuse --gpg-homedir in a verify of sign and summary.
  * Write the dependencies of a commit with commit --related. Pull,
    push, receive, and static deltas carry the dependencies. Prune keeps
    the related commits, and fsck reports dependency errors.
  * Remove the config keys gc-root-metadata-keys and
    detached-metadata-exclude. Add the config key keep-detached-related.
  * Read the verification keys of the remote in pull-local. Add the
    pull-local options --sign-verify, --sign-verify-summary,
    --no-gpg-verify, --no-gpg-verify-summary, --no-sign-verify,
    --no-sign-verify-summary, and --trust.
  * Take the commit keys of a pull from the trust group that the remote
    key trust names.
  * Read each regular file of a gpgkeypath directory. Read the global
    trusted directory when the remote has no keyring.
  * Add send --one-way and receive --one-way.
  * Reach an origin through a socks5 or a socks5h proxy.

 -- Alexey Naidyonov <alexey.naidyonov@gmail.com>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 17:00:09 +0100

ostrya (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Store the composefs image of a commit as a .cfs object. commit
    --generate-composefs stores the image. Add composefs-image. Prune
    removes the image with its commit, and fsck checks each image.
  * Carry the composefs image in pull, push, send, serve, and static
    deltas.
  * Write each ref into the root summary, and write the summary of the
    anonymous item under extensions/ostrya/summary/.
  * Add summary -c/--client-groups.
  * State archive-z2 in each served summary.
  * Keep the summary of the anonymous item served after a mirror pull.
  * Start a plain HTTP serve next to an HTTPS serve of one repository.
  * Add the template unit ostrya-serve@.service and the sysusers.d file of
    the user ostrya. Build ostrya-mountd from its own source package.

